  "body": "Sam Altman is a backer of Induced AI, a startup founded this year by two teenagers that automates business workflows by converting plain English instructions to pseudo-code in real time. At its annual hardware event, Google announced updates to the Pixel 8, Pixel 8 Pro, Pixel Fold, Android 14, Pixel Buds, Google Assistant, Bard, and Pixel Watch 2. A review of the Pixel 8 Pro notes it is similar to the Pixel 7 Pro but offers improved cameras, a brighter screen, and enhanced AI features, though it has an underutilized temperature sensor. Dave Clark, ousted as Flexport CEO just a year into his job, criticized the company's founder and board following CNBC reporting on his departure; Flexport is valued at $8 billion. A book by Michael Lewis, 'Going Infinite,' debuted on the first day of Sam Bankman-Fried's Manhattan Federal Court trial, revealing details about SBF's attempt to buy off Trump to prevent him from running for president again. Prosecutors in the SBF trial accused Bankman-Fried of knowingly committing fraud for wealth and power, while the defense argued he acted in good faith and got over his head. LinkedIn launched AI tools for job hunting, marketing, and sales, including an updated Recruiter platform, an AI Learning coach, and a marketing campaign tool. Elon Musk claimed X generated 100–200 million daily posts in September, while CEO Linda Yaccarino later stated the figure was 500 million posts per day. IronNet, founded in 2014 by former NSA director Keith Alexander, laid off staff after failing to gain traction post-IPO in August 2021 despite raising over $400 million. Esther Rodriguez-Villegas from Acurable, a medical device company making wearables for sleep apnea and epilepsy, explains existing devices make detecting and treating these conditions difficult. Breathe Battery Technologies created software that can be added to lithium-ion batteries to enable faster charging or greater longevity. A survey of 10 investors highlighted where startups can succeed, the impact of oligopoly dynamics, and the value of proprietary data in the future of AI. Gmail announced stricter rules for bulk senders starting next year."
